<p>North Korea fired several short-range ballistic missiles from near Wonsan on its east coast on Wednesday, according to South Korea’s military, in the latest sign of tension on the Korean Peninsula. South Korean officials said the missiles flew toward the sea to the east. A day earlier, one projectile appeared to run into problems soon after launch and then disappeared, according to reports citing military assessments. The launches came as Pyongyang publicly rejected hopes of better relations with Seoul. Reports said North Korea dismissed South Korea’s diplomatic outreach and signaled it had no intention of resuming reconciliation efforts. South Korea and the United States were analyzing the launches, a reminder of how quickly political hopes can give way to renewed military signaling even as regional monitoring and coordination continue.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/vaY7phmyPu8PPVddXhsdJ5J7ZS4NdC7PpItiy6hWgTVDRWixaN6ty8a_UOYXhqeqKfrnfhATklCVqooSc7ySzGjy3mPk7_jrKgOI1b71xH1gukRruf2iN7FZJxIu3LnxST1wvbq89Ta1KAgbG8a-DmzCaGXqyGZP9P3zyEdibg' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Launch timing: South Korea’s Joint Chiefs of Staff said Wednesday’s missiles were fired at about 8:50 a.m. from near Wonsan on North Korea’s east coast.</li><li>Flight distance: The missiles traveled about 240 kilometers, or roughly 150 miles, according to the Joint Chiefs of Staff.</li><li>Test count: SCMP said Wednesday’s launch was North Korea’s fifth missile test since Seoul’s latest efforts to seek calmer ties.</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/north-korea-fires-suspected-missiles-as-pyongyang-dismisses-seouls-diplomacy-hopes/article70836882.ece'>North Korea fires suspected missiles as Pyongyang dismisses Seoul’s diplomacy hopes</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/north-korea-fires-ballistic-missiles-toward-sea/a-76700950'>North Korea fires ballistic missiles toward sea</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='ht